WEBVTT

00:48.674 --> 00:50.300
They're so beautiful, Tom.

00:57.349 --> 00:58.600
God.

00:58.684 --> 01:00.102
- Oh, no.
- What?

01:01.228 --> 01:02.229
Left out my poem.

01:02.312 --> 01:03.939
Oh, no.

01:04.565 --> 01:05.566
Unbelievable.

01:06.233 --> 01:08.819
I went over the layout with her
three times.

01:08.902 --> 01:12.906
But you know, these things happen.
So, don't… don't be too hard on her.

01:13.740 --> 01:14.992
Yeah, I guess you're right.

01:19.955 --> 01:21.290
Read it again.

01:27.004 --> 01:29.339
"New England's Best Kept Secret."

01:29.423 --> 01:30.632
Not for long.

01:31.758 --> 01:33.594
"Don't look for a Starbucks here."

01:33.677 --> 01:36.013
Skip ahead
to the part about Martha's Vineyard.

01:38.348 --> 01:41.602
"Widow's Bay
is the next Martha's Vineyard."

01:43.937 --> 01:44.938
That's all it says about that.

01:45.022 --> 01:46.315
- Yeah, I know.
- It's not really a "part."

01:46.398 --> 01:47.649
All right, just keep reading.

02:03.874 --> 02:04.875
Now, this…

02:06.168 --> 02:07.169
this…

02:07.252 --> 02:09.378
this is what
Widow's Bay should taste like.

02:09.963 --> 02:10.964
Really.

02:11.048 --> 02:13.550
Took a while to figure out how to use it.

02:13.634 --> 02:15.802
Well, it was worth it.

02:16.386 --> 02:19.556
It's just… nobody's ordering it.

02:20.933 --> 02:22.392
I put a lot into this, Tom.

02:22.476 --> 02:23.810
- I don't know--
- I know. I know.

02:23.894 --> 02:26.313
And you're gonna make
your money back and then some.

02:26.396 --> 02:30.776
The tourists are coming this weekend,
and then word will spread.

02:30.859 --> 02:32.528
Lot of opportunity coming your wa…

02:38.784 --> 02:40.786
Wyck, so long buddy.

02:42.913 --> 02:44.289
Bechir, what the hell's going on?

02:45.207 --> 02:46.208
Hey. Hey!

02:46.291 --> 02:48.418
That's my livelihood, you son of a bitch!

02:48.502 --> 02:50.379
I am not a son of a bitch!

02:50.462 --> 02:52.339
I just got this place ready,
and we're fully booked.

02:52.422 --> 02:53.632
All right, Wyck.

02:53.715 --> 02:55.008
Let's get you some coffee.

02:55.092 --> 02:57.261
No, you can't let people stay here.

02:57.344 --> 02:58.345
Not the inn.

02:58.428 --> 03:01.723
The inn is not right!

03:01.807 --> 03:03.600
Wyck! Wyck! Wyck, come on!

03:03.684 --> 03:05.060
- I got here first!
- Oh, my God.

03:05.143 --> 03:06.520
- No. No!
- Wyck.

03:07.563 --> 03:08.564
Be careful!

03:11.400 --> 03:12.526
You okay?

03:16.113 --> 03:18.490
All right, Wyck. Let's go sleep it off.

03:18.574 --> 03:20.617
No! No, no, no.

03:20.701 --> 03:24.413
The inn is haunted.

03:24.496 --> 03:25.581
And your mayor…

03:25.664 --> 03:28.125
your mayor is a fool.

03:28.208 --> 03:30.419
- Leave him alone, Loftis.
- Yeah, leave him alone.

03:30.502 --> 03:32.671
- He's harmless.
- …gonna get us all killed.

03:32.754 --> 03:35.340
Yeah, he doesn't care about us.
He's selfish.

03:35.424 --> 03:37.718
He's a selfish fool!

03:37.801 --> 03:39.136
No.

03:39.219 --> 03:40.470
All right.

03:44.683 --> 03:45.851
Okay, folks. You know what?

03:45.934 --> 03:47.811
I think we're gonna let him
cool down for a little while.

03:47.895 --> 03:49.188
How is he able to roll down the window?

03:49.271 --> 03:51.607
- 'Cause he's not in cuffs.
- He'd never set foot inside

03:51.690 --> 03:53.025
- by himself.
- Of course, I would.

03:53.108 --> 03:54.484
No, you can't trust him.

03:54.568 --> 03:56.236
He's only doing it for the money!

03:56.320 --> 03:57.654
Of course, I'm not doing it for the money!

03:57.738 --> 03:59.656
- I'm looking out for all of us.
- 'Cause he's not one of us.

03:59.740 --> 04:00.741
He's a coward!

04:00.824 --> 04:02.284
Fuck you, you dumb hick!

04:08.540 --> 04:12.294
- Oh. I'm a hick. You see what I mean?
- I… I didn't…

04:12.377 --> 04:14.546
- I obviously didn't…
- You all heard him say it!

04:14.630 --> 04:17.007
You heard him say what he said!

04:17.089 --> 04:18.382
- I…
- You heard him!

04:18.466 --> 04:21.928
I am not a hick!

04:25.641 --> 04:27.809
Where are we going? I don't wanna go!

04:27.893 --> 04:29.353
He just needs to sleep it off.

04:31.980 --> 04:33.398
Thank you, everyone.

04:36.193 --> 04:38.362
- Unbelievable.
- Just a circus.

04:52.251 --> 04:53.669
Hey, Ginny. Just picking up.

05:01.343 --> 05:03.345
Well, I heard you had quite a day.

05:04.555 --> 05:05.556
You heard?

05:06.932 --> 05:09.685
You know how hard it
was to get that article?

05:09.768 --> 05:10.853
I know, I know.

05:10.936 --> 05:12.688
Not an ounce of gratitude.

05:12.771 --> 05:14.690
And that fucking guy…

05:14.773 --> 05:18.443
Oh, you know Wyck
has not had the easiest go of it.

05:19.653 --> 05:22.489
So he just gets to do
whatever the hell he wants

05:22.573 --> 05:23.866
and people just love him?

05:25.284 --> 05:27.286
Well, you know
people around here fear change.

05:28.495 --> 05:31.999
And when the Lord gathers a herd,

05:33.166 --> 05:34.459
he calls a shepherd.

05:38.046 --> 05:40.048
Oh, so you're just phoning it in now.

05:40.132 --> 05:42.759
- Oh, right.
- Sure, I guess. James 4:6 though.

05:42.843 --> 05:44.928
Blah, blah, Bible, Bible, you know.

05:45.012 --> 05:46.013
Right.

05:46.763 --> 05:48.473
You wanna come by for a drink?

05:48.557 --> 05:50.684
- Picking up for Evan.
- Okay, next time.

05:50.767 --> 05:51.768
Next time.

05:52.436 --> 05:54.104
Oh, hey…

05:56.398 --> 05:58.233
You should probably
keep the doors locked at night.

05:59.359 --> 06:00.444
- Pardon?
- The bell.

06:00.527 --> 06:03.071
I mean, let's be honest, it probably
was Evan and I will talk to him.

06:03.155 --> 06:05.073
But we both know that won't do any good.

06:05.157 --> 06:07.159
- The bell… The church bell?
- Yeah.

06:07.242 --> 06:09.203
Woke up Rosemary and Patricia too.

06:10.871 --> 06:12.331
Tom, that's impossible.

06:12.414 --> 06:13.832
Oh, you haven't met my son.

06:17.127 --> 06:18.128
You okay?

06:19.796 --> 06:21.173
Yeah, I'm fine.

06:22.758 --> 06:23.759
Go home to your boy.

06:30.599 --> 06:32.226
Did Kathy bag this?

06:32.309 --> 06:33.977
No, I bagged it.

06:36.522 --> 06:37.689
Thank you.

06:43.695 --> 06:44.696
"Dumb hick."

06:57.835 --> 06:58.877
I didn't mean that.

06:58.961 --> 07:00.295
I really didn't.

07:00.379 --> 07:01.880
And I know you're…

07:02.923 --> 07:04.424
you're all loyal to Wyck,

07:05.300 --> 07:06.927
but that doesn't make him right.

07:08.053 --> 07:13.642
We have a new chapter now,
and there is nothing wrong with that inn.

07:13.725 --> 07:15.477
A lot of bad things have gone down there.

07:15.561 --> 07:17.729
Yes, that's true.

07:18.313 --> 07:19.690
But it doesn't make it haunted.

07:19.773 --> 07:21.692
I would never put anyone in danger.

07:21.775 --> 07:23.110
Then why don't you stay there?

07:25.195 --> 07:27.114
Are you gonna pay for my room, Al?

07:27.197 --> 07:30.158
- We'll all chip in.
- Yeah.

07:30.242 --> 07:31.660
Great. I look forward to it.

07:33.287 --> 07:34.288
Tonight.

07:35.664 --> 07:38.041
Guys, I have my son at home.

07:42.671 --> 07:44.047
Nice excuse.

07:47.676 --> 07:49.011
Okay, I'll do it.

07:49.553 --> 07:52.598
If that's what it takes,
I will stay there tonight.

07:52.681 --> 07:54.683
You have to stay in the Captain's Suite.

07:54.766 --> 07:55.767
The what?

07:55.851 --> 07:57.060
Lost his mind.

07:57.561 --> 07:58.979
Got his family with an axe.

07:59.062 --> 08:01.273
Of course we then named a suite after him.

08:01.356 --> 08:04.735
- Anything else?
- "The Ungrateful Hortence Fitzgerald."

08:04.818 --> 08:06.987
Was she the lady who fell out of a window?

08:07.070 --> 08:08.572
Ugly woman who fled her wedding.

08:08.655 --> 08:10.949
Backed through a window
and fell to her death.

08:11.033 --> 08:14.703
If you say "ugly Hortence" three times,
you will see her ungrateful reflection.

08:15.746 --> 08:18.415
You know, I'm gonna ask that
we start questioning these narratives.

08:18.498 --> 08:21.418
There's misogyny in the air.
More than a whiff.

08:21.919 --> 08:24.087
- You're not writing these down.
- Oh, sorry.

08:24.171 --> 08:26.965
- Oh, New Years Eve, 1962, disaster.
- Yeah.

08:27.049 --> 08:29.092
John Reynold's head in the dumbwaiter.

08:29.176 --> 08:30.594
That clown killer of '51.

08:30.677 --> 08:32.763
Oh, yeah.
This was a guy who killed clowns?

08:32.846 --> 08:34.597
No, it was a murderer
who dressed as a clown!

08:34.681 --> 08:36.058
Oh, sorry.

08:36.140 --> 08:39.186
He should spend time in that crawl space.

08:39.269 --> 08:40.354
Yeah.

08:40.979 --> 08:42.397
Thank you, Rosemary.

08:42.481 --> 08:45.275
All the way to the back too.
Not halfway, pussy.

08:45.359 --> 08:46.693
Not a problem. Anything else?

08:46.777 --> 08:48.278
He's not gonna spend
the whole night there.

08:49.446 --> 08:50.739
Kurt could lock him in.

08:53.951 --> 08:55.202
Okay, I'll do it.

08:55.285 --> 09:00.040
But when I do, all this talk stops, right?

09:00.541 --> 09:01.542
You let it go.

09:02.042 --> 09:04.086
You let tourists stay there in peace.

09:04.586 --> 09:05.587
Agreed?

09:06.547 --> 09:08.841
Yeah, I guess. Yeah. Sure.

09:09.508 --> 09:10.968
All right. Thank you.

09:14.096 --> 09:15.097
Don't do it.

10:08.442 --> 10:11.278
Excellent.
Bob's at 9 to 7 in the bottom of the 7.

10:12.196 --> 10:14.823
Boston hoping to keep the deficit to 2.

10:16.450 --> 10:19.411
Listen, I…
I have to stay at the inn tonight

10:19.494 --> 10:22.831
to make sure everything is
in order for the tourists.

10:23.957 --> 10:25.876
Wait, tour… tourists are actually coming?

10:26.877 --> 10:28.795
Yes. So…

10:31.256 --> 10:33.008
you're gonna spend the night at Ruth's.

10:34.051 --> 10:35.052
No.

10:36.553 --> 10:37.679
Fuck no.

10:37.763 --> 10:40.807
No. Come on. She's so old. Please.

10:40.891 --> 10:42.267
Please. I don't wanna go.

10:42.351 --> 10:43.352
Sorry.

10:48.857 --> 10:49.858
Actually, it's fine.

10:52.361 --> 10:54.029
- Wait, wait. What did you just concoct?
- Huh?

10:54.112 --> 10:55.572
- What? I'm gonna go pack.
- No,

10:55.656 --> 10:57.866
this will not be an excuse
for you to go out…

10:57.950 --> 10:59.701
- Don't eat my sandwich!
- …at all hou…

11:00.202 --> 11:03.330
I'm gonna be calling there
and checking in throughout the night!

11:18.053 --> 11:19.638
This place freaks me out.

11:21.181 --> 11:22.182
Okay, good luck!

12:11.481 --> 12:13.859
I took down some of
the more provocative ones, like you asked.

12:14.985 --> 12:16.987
This isn't provocative?

12:22.618 --> 12:23.619
What's that?

12:23.702 --> 12:24.786
They want you to film it.

12:25.787 --> 12:27.664
They say it's the only way
they'll know for sure.

12:27.748 --> 12:28.999
Okay.

12:29.082 --> 12:32.878
Well, give me the keys
to the Captain's Suite.

12:38.217 --> 12:40.719
There's a honor bar in the parlor.

12:40.802 --> 12:43.472
You sign your name
on the form and say what you drank.

12:43.555 --> 12:45.265
- Got it.
- There's a security camera

12:45.349 --> 12:47.226
so I'll know
if you don't log what you took.

12:48.268 --> 12:49.770
That's not really an honor system.

12:59.196 --> 13:01.365
Marie gave it a quick turnover today.

13:02.032 --> 13:06.119
There's no AC, but she did put
a fan on the desk for climate control.

13:07.037 --> 13:09.540
There's two chairs, your choice.

13:10.165 --> 13:15.546
Some local sundries
and linens and soaps in the bathroom.

13:16.129 --> 13:18.549
You don't bring the bags in
for the guests?

13:20.467 --> 13:21.468
Shit.

13:31.353 --> 13:32.771
I'll be reachable at home if you need me.

13:32.855 --> 13:34.439
Wait, you don't stay here?

13:35.065 --> 13:37.067
What if a guest needs something?

13:37.150 --> 13:38.986
Then they can reach me at home.

13:40.988 --> 13:41.989
Night.

13:47.160 --> 13:48.161
Night.

14:23.864 --> 14:24.865
Well,

14:24.948 --> 14:27.367
I don't understand
why we can't just leave end of July.

14:27.451 --> 14:28.452
Thanks.

14:29.036 --> 14:31.622
Well, we'll be outta here by Labor Day.

14:32.247 --> 14:33.749
Loftis asks for too much.

14:33.832 --> 14:36.126
Listen. I know, I know.

14:38.754 --> 14:39.755
Get some sleep.

14:40.589 --> 14:41.590
Love you.

14:43.759 --> 14:45.344
Moving somewhere?

14:51.475 --> 14:52.726
Soon as I can.

14:55.354 --> 14:56.355
Smart.

15:13.288 --> 15:14.873
Welcome to Widow's Bay.

15:14.957 --> 15:16.583
There's so much to see here.

15:17.543 --> 15:19.795
Come with me, I'll show you around.

15:37.229 --> 15:38.313
What?

17:20.958 --> 17:22.542
Fill out the form.

17:48.777 --> 17:50.946
Ugly Hortence.

17:51.446 --> 17:53.365
Ugly Hortence.

17:53.991 --> 17:56.952
Ugly Hortence.

18:17.681 --> 18:22.144
One, two, three, four, five.

18:26.899 --> 18:28.734
Come the fuck on!

19:06.980 --> 19:08.190
Not a chance.

19:18.617 --> 19:19.618
Hello.

19:20.619 --> 19:22.079
Hi. Hi, Ruth. It's Tom.

19:22.162 --> 19:23.705
Just checking in on Evan.

19:23.789 --> 19:25.165
Oh, hi, Tom.

19:25.249 --> 19:26.250
I'll go find him.

19:26.875 --> 19:27.918
Great. Thank you.

19:28.001 --> 19:29.002
Evan?

19:30.003 --> 19:31.004
Evan?

19:31.880 --> 19:33.715
Evan, your daddy's on the phone.

19:34.550 --> 19:36.677
Evan, it's your daddy.

19:40.973 --> 19:42.474
Oh. I didn't know I left this pie on.

19:42.558 --> 19:46.186
Oh, my gosh. Oh. Didn't do much damage.

19:46.770 --> 19:47.771
Okay.

20:24.725 --> 20:28.478
Eight, seven, six, five,

20:28.562 --> 20:31.398
four, three, two, one.

20:31.481 --> 20:34.234
Happy New Year!

21:26.912 --> 21:27.913
Hello?

21:30.666 --> 21:31.667
Hello?

21:40.300 --> 21:41.301
Hello?

21:44.137 --> 21:46.431
I mean, I'm s… Who are you?

21:46.515 --> 21:48.517
What are you… What are you doing here?

21:49.101 --> 21:50.227
What are you doing here?

21:51.937 --> 21:54.231
The innkeeper didn't tell me
anyone else would be here.

21:55.524 --> 21:57.401
Does he usually
announce guests to each other?

21:58.360 --> 21:59.444
Oh, my God.

22:00.279 --> 22:01.572
I'm William.

22:03.448 --> 22:04.658
I'm Tom.

22:04.741 --> 22:08.161
You all right?
You seem like you could use a drink.

22:08.245 --> 22:10.873
- There's an honor bar downstairs.
- No, thank you.

22:11.540 --> 22:12.833
I mean, thanks, but…

22:16.545 --> 22:17.546
Good night.

22:49.369 --> 22:50.704
Come with me.

22:52.414 --> 22:53.415
Fuck!

22:55.334 --> 22:56.752
You okay, neighbor?

22:58.879 --> 23:00.547
The camera is for what?

23:03.467 --> 23:05.802
You know what?
I c… I can't even get into it.

23:10.807 --> 23:12.809
You know, I've been to Widow's Bay before.

23:12.893 --> 23:15.312
For fuck's sake, it was nice
to order a cappuccino for once.

23:16.897 --> 23:18.190
Yes.

23:18.273 --> 23:19.358
Tha… Thank you.

23:19.441 --> 23:20.609
God.

23:20.692 --> 23:22.528
Feels good to hear someone say that.

23:24.488 --> 23:26.490
So… So what brings you here this time?

23:26.573 --> 23:28.700
Oh, I work
for a structural engineering firm.

23:28.784 --> 23:31.411
- City hired us to inspect the dock.
- Right.

23:31.495 --> 23:33.372
Yeah. For the expansion.

23:33.455 --> 23:36.291
Yeah. Looks like you're expecting
a lot more ferries out here, huh?

23:36.792 --> 23:37.876
It's the hope.

23:38.377 --> 23:40.128
Well, that's a lot on your shoulders.

23:40.212 --> 23:42.130
I'm sure your constituents are excited.

23:44.174 --> 23:45.175
No?

23:46.552 --> 23:47.761
They don't make it easy.

23:48.720 --> 23:50.973
Well, they must appreciate you some.

23:51.056 --> 23:52.474
They voted you in as mayor.

23:55.102 --> 23:56.895
I ran uncontested.

23:59.022 --> 24:00.274
That's embarrassing, Tom.

24:05.320 --> 24:07.197
All right. Testing my luck.

24:09.491 --> 24:12.327
- Oh! No. No.
- Okay. Here we go.

24:12.411 --> 24:15.122
"Uh-oh. Daddy's younger boss
yelled at him today."

24:16.206 --> 24:17.291
- What?
- What?

24:18.208 --> 24:19.877
Now I gotta go back three spaces.

24:19.960 --> 24:23.255
- All right. You're up. There you go.
- Okay.

24:23.922 --> 24:26.175
"Roll… Roll to see
if the neighbor is home."

24:27.384 --> 24:28.385
Come on, neighbor.

24:29.595 --> 24:30.971
Yes!

24:31.054 --> 24:32.389
Saved by the neighbor.

24:32.472 --> 24:34.016
One. Two. Three. Four.

24:34.099 --> 24:35.100
Thanks, man.

24:35.184 --> 24:36.977
Here we go.

24:37.853 --> 24:39.188
"Daddy had a bad day.

24:39.271 --> 24:41.690
- Go back six spaces."
- Oh, man. I'm in the basement.

24:43.108 --> 24:44.610
I'm getting crushed.

24:48.697 --> 24:50.490
Yeah, he was a local.

24:50.574 --> 24:52.576
My mom was from the mainland.

24:53.410 --> 24:55.370
They met when she was on a schooner tour.

24:55.454 --> 24:56.455
Uh-huh.

24:56.538 --> 24:58.957
But she certainly
couldn't make it work with him.

24:59.041 --> 25:02.669
So, I grew up in,
I grew up in Massachusetts.

25:02.753 --> 25:04.755
But I spent my summers here.

25:07.049 --> 25:08.967
I used to dread those summers.

25:09.051 --> 25:10.469
- Really?
- Yeah.

25:10.552 --> 25:11.929
How bad was he?

25:14.598 --> 25:15.599
I mean…

25:17.309 --> 25:18.644
not the worst guy in the world.

25:18.727 --> 25:22.397
Just a lot of…
walking on egg shells, you know?

25:22.481 --> 25:23.649
Oh, I do.

25:24.733 --> 25:26.860
Didn't talk much once I got older.

25:27.569 --> 25:29.029
Moved back when he got sick.

25:29.988 --> 25:30.989
Met my wife.

25:31.990 --> 25:33.200
Rest is history.

25:34.243 --> 25:36.036
Guy's lucky you came back at all.

25:36.119 --> 25:37.120
Yeah.

25:42.668 --> 25:45.671
You know, just a lot of the times he would
come home after a couple of drinks,

25:45.754 --> 25:47.005
spewing these…

25:49.466 --> 25:52.594
just these horror stories
about the island.

25:52.678 --> 25:54.012
I mean shit I was…

25:54.513 --> 25:56.014
I was way too young to hear.

25:59.268 --> 26:00.978
The guy never should've had a kid.

26:05.190 --> 26:07.192
He called me soft when I was six.

26:13.866 --> 26:18.120
I always said, you know, the only thing
this island's cursed with is alcoholism.

26:21.874 --> 26:23.125
You gotta be careful.

26:24.877 --> 26:27.296
They'll drag you down with them
if you let 'em.

26:29.089 --> 26:33.552
Fuckin' useless ass-backwards,
small brained, townie hicks.

26:34.720 --> 26:39.474
Let 'em all rot in hell
and watch 'em all fucking burn.

26:47.357 --> 26:48.692
I may have had too much to drink.

26:54.281 --> 26:57.326
Listen. I know two things to be true.

26:57.826 --> 26:59.745
One, you're a great mayor.

27:00.370 --> 27:01.455
No, no, no. Uh-uh.

27:03.332 --> 27:04.625
I know these things.

27:04.708 --> 27:05.709
And two,

27:06.919 --> 27:09.213
there's no such thing as ghosts.
All right?

27:09.296 --> 27:11.048
There's no… what was it?

27:11.131 --> 27:12.299
"Harriet Fitzgerald"?

27:12.883 --> 27:14.468
- Hortence.
- Well, okay.

27:15.052 --> 27:17.554
No Hortence is going to appear
in your window.

27:17.638 --> 27:19.139
You know, the killer sea captain,

27:19.223 --> 27:20.807
the New Year's party,

27:20.891 --> 27:22.559
the "murder clown," I mean…

27:23.936 --> 27:27.731
Maybe all those things were real
at one point, but they're not anymore.

27:28.315 --> 27:29.316
So…

27:30.317 --> 27:32.069
All right. To bed.

27:33.237 --> 27:34.446
I say,

27:35.447 --> 27:38.450
you finish off their little checklist
and show 'em who's in charge.

27:39.368 --> 27:40.369
Cheers.

27:41.411 --> 27:42.579
Cheers.

27:45.749 --> 27:47.376
Well, probably best.

27:48.168 --> 27:49.837
Okay. All right.

27:50.504 --> 27:51.547
Have a good one.

27:51.630 --> 27:52.798
- Night.
- Night.

27:59.346 --> 28:00.347
I'm good.

29:33.649 --> 29:36.151
I am in the crawl space.

29:43.909 --> 29:44.910
Hello?

29:50.707 --> 29:51.959
William?

29:56.004 --> 29:57.089
William?

30:03.011 --> 30:04.012
Howdy, neighbor.

30:05.347 --> 30:07.808
Wha… Why didn't you answer me?

30:14.565 --> 30:15.899
Need some help in there?

30:15.983 --> 30:18.110
What? No! No.

30:18.861 --> 30:20.571
No, don't… don't… don't come in.

30:20.654 --> 30:21.697
Don't… I'm coming out!

30:21.780 --> 30:23.407
Don't come in! Don't come…

30:27.953 --> 30:29.329
Oh, no!

30:42.009 --> 30:43.093
I locked the door myself.

30:43.177 --> 30:45.429
Whoever it was
would've had to have had a key, Tom.

30:45.512 --> 30:46.513
What…

30:47.264 --> 30:48.265
He's…

30:49.016 --> 30:50.934
Oh, did you see something? You…

30:51.018 --> 30:52.895
Oh, you didn't see anyone
in the crawl space, huh?

30:52.978 --> 30:54.646
Well, does my demeanor suggest

30:54.730 --> 30:56.899
that I just engaged with someone
inside a crawl space?

30:58.066 --> 30:59.067
Hold on.

31:11.079 --> 31:14.750
I don't understand. Now look…
maybe I was… I was…

31:15.250 --> 31:16.251
sleepwalking?

31:16.335 --> 31:17.336
I know. Oh, my…

31:17.836 --> 31:19.630
He said his name was William.

31:19.713 --> 31:20.797
Willy.

31:21.548 --> 31:22.966
The clown.

31:23.675 --> 31:24.885
That's who you got, huh?

31:25.511 --> 31:26.678
You saw something.

31:27.846 --> 31:32.059
You saw something and
you're still gonna let folks stay here.

31:32.809 --> 31:34.603
- Don't you start with this shit, Wyck.
- No.

31:34.686 --> 31:36.855
- Don't you raise your voice at me.
- Shit. Every cent I have

31:36.939 --> 31:39.066
- I put into this inn!
- I'm telling you this place is a trap!

31:39.149 --> 31:40.442
It's not!

31:40.526 --> 31:42.152
It's perfectly fine.

31:42.236 --> 31:44.404
Then you go in the Captain's Suite.

31:46.615 --> 31:47.616
Kurt, just…

31:49.493 --> 31:53.330
just go into the room and show him
there's nothing to be afraid of.

31:55.916 --> 31:58.085
There. See?

31:59.169 --> 32:00.170
Inside.

32:00.796 --> 32:03.924
- What?
- Go inside and close the door.

32:05.217 --> 32:07.261
We're gonna… we're gonna count to ten.

32:13.642 --> 32:15.310
One, two, three, four, five,

32:15.394 --> 32:17.312
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

32:18.689 --> 32:20.482
What the fuck?
I thought we said ten seconds?

32:20.566 --> 32:21.650
Well, that was ten.

32:21.733 --> 32:23.485
How long do you think you were in there?

32:25.988 --> 32:28.740
- Ten seconds.
- Then why don't you go back in for 30?

32:28.824 --> 32:30.534
Can I at least have some food first?

32:30.617 --> 32:32.619
The fuck you need food for 30 seconds for?

32:38.709 --> 32:42.462
Loftis, you know there's
something wrong with this island.

32:42.546 --> 32:45.382
You've seen it with your own two eyes now.

32:46.133 --> 32:47.176
Come on, son.

32:48.135 --> 32:49.761
You're right here with me.

32:49.845 --> 32:51.096
Seeing what I'm seeing.

32:53.390 --> 32:54.933
You can call it off right now.

32:58.937 --> 32:59.980
No, I can't.

33:00.063 --> 33:01.148
We can.

33:02.191 --> 33:05.444
It's not right to bring anyone here,
you know it.

33:05.527 --> 33:06.862
Island's awake now.

33:06.945 --> 33:08.405
It's dangerous.

33:08.989 --> 33:09.990
All right.

33:16.246 --> 33:17.247
All set?

33:36.308 --> 33:38.268
What the hell is this?

33:44.316 --> 33:45.734
This black mold?

33:50.447 --> 33:51.573
Mold.

33:54.034 --> 33:56.453
Well, that's it, you must
have hallucinated from exposure.

33:56.537 --> 33:57.538
No.

33:58.080 --> 33:59.414
No.

34:00.624 --> 34:04.711
You think you could
get affected that quickly? No.

34:04.795 --> 34:08.005
That can be remediated in 72 hours, Tom.

34:08.090 --> 34:11.009
And I will still seal up
this suite for good measure.

34:16.473 --> 34:17.641
Loftis.

34:49.840 --> 34:50.841
How'd it go?

34:51.592 --> 34:52.592
Fine.
